      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sdge:cc-tou-dr1-2026-04-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sdge:cc-tou-dr1-2026-04-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "The most consequential gap is inside a charge the filing does model. Schedule TOU-DR1 publishes the Baseline Adjustment Credit as $(0.10892) per kWh for usage up to 130 percent of baseline, with the quantities given in Special Condition 15 (Basic Allowance 9.0, 10.4, 13.6 and 15.9 kWh per day in summer for the Coastal, Inland, Mountain and Desert zones and 9.2, 9.6, 12.9 and 10.9 in winter, plus a separate All Electric set), and Sheet 2 note (4) ties the credit to that cap. This filing carries the credit as a single price with no tier or bound, so it is applied to every kWh; a high-usage customer's bill computed from this data will be too low, and the published allowance quantities appear nowhere. Four further provisions are absent. The TOU-DR1-MB table on Sheet 3, whose total effective Medical Baseline rates run from $0.29919 per kWh summer super off-peak to $0.54054 summer on-peak with DWR-BC and WF-NBC at zero; no SDG&E Medical Baseline overlay exists in this corpus. The Franchise Fee Differential of 5.78 percent for customers within the corporate limits of the City of San Diego. The semi-annual California Climate Credit of $49.36 under Schedule GHG-ARR. And Special Condition 12 Bill Protection, a credit for the difference where a migrating customer's twelve-month total on this schedule exceeds what Schedule DR would have cost; note that the tariff closes this to new customers, stating that a customer taking service on or after March 1, 2019 does not receive it. The TOU-DR1-CARE column on Sheet 2 and the DRAH and FERA Base Services Charges of $0.39688 per day are carried by separate overlay filings rather than missing. Special Conditions 1, 6, 7, 8, 10 and 11 (interval metering, meter ownership and reads, multiple-account billing, standard lighting voltage and welder ratings) are metering and service terms, not rates; the Special Condition 9 bar on returning to the schedule for 12 months after leaving is an enrollment rule and is likewise not expressed.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
